<title>USA: Wilmington set to manage Clemente Global.</title>
<headline>Wilmington set to manage Clemente Global.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Clemente Capital Inc said it nominated Wilmington Trust Co to manage the U.S. portion of its $62 million closed-end global growth fund.</p>
<p>The fund also announced that Robert Christian, chief financial officer of Wilmington, was nominated to the fund's board, and Thomas Prepas, chief economist of Clemente Capital, was appointed portfolio manager of the non-U.S. portion of the fund.</p>
<p>Wilmington bought 24 percent of Clemente Capital last April.</p>
